diff --git a/docfx/docs/drawing.md b/docfx/docs/drawing.md
index b081fac..e28e64e 100644
--- a/docfx/docs/drawing.md
+++ b/docfx/docs/drawing.md
@@ -68,6 +68,14 @@ When `View.Draw()` is called on a view that has <xref:Terminal.Gui.ViewBase.View
 9. **Cache Clip for Margin** — If the <xref:Terminal.Gui.ViewBase.Margin> has a shadow, the current clip is cached for the second-pass shadow render.
 10. **DrawComplete & Clip Exclusion** — Raises `DrawComplete`. For opaque views, the entire frame is excluded from the clip. For transparent views, only the actually-drawn cells are excluded. This ensures later-drawn (lower-Z) views don't overwrite this view's content.
 
+### SubView-Only Redraws
+
+A view that has `SubViewNeedsDraw` set but not <xref:Terminal.Gui.ViewBase.View.NeedsDraw> (only a SubView is dirty) does **not** escalate into a full redraw of itself. Steps 1, 3, 5, 6 and 7 are skipped: its adornments, viewport, text and content are left as they are on screen, and only the dirty SubViews are drawn. Clean SubViews are not drawn at all (no `Draw`/`DrawComplete`), but the area they own is still excluded from the clip so dirty lower-Z peers can't overwrite them. For Overlapped SubViews with `SuperViewRendersLineCanvas = true` (e.g. `Tabs` pages), each SubView's last resolved <xref:Terminal.Gui.Drawing.LineCanvas> cells are cached so the painters'-algorithm composite stays correct without redrawing clean peers.
+
+The view falls back to a full redraw when a dirty SubView depends on the SuperView repainting beneath it or re-composing its <xref:Terminal.Gui.Drawing.LineCanvas>: a transparent viewport, a transparent Margin or a shadow; a changed screen frame; a tiled `SuperViewRendersLineCanvas` SubView; or a dirty SubView of one of the view's own adornments. A dirty SubView with a transparent Border/Padding (such as a tab page) is allowed. After it draws, the view checks that it still covers every cell it covered before. If it doesn't, the view redraws fully in the same pass so no stale cells are left.
+
+If you clear the screen outside the normal main loop (e.g. `IDriver.ClearContents ()` in a test), call `SetNeedsDraw ()` on the top view as well, just as the application does when forcing a redraw.
+
 ### Peer-View Draw Loop
 
 The static `View.Draw(views, force)` method orchestrates drawing a set of peer views (views sharing the same SuperView):
